 need to know:\n\n### **The Three Export Systems**\n\n- **System A (Ardent)**: Comment preamble, ISO dates (YYYY-MM-DD), amounts in decimal dollars, quoted fields with embedded delimiters allowed\n- **System B (Borough)**: Plain format, ISO dates, **amounts in integer cents** (e.g., `25440` = $254.40), every row starts with system letter 'B', no quoting\n- **System C (Calder)**: Banner + header + rows + trailer, dates in **dd/mm/yyyy** format (day first!), decimal dollars, trailer has row count\n\nThe parsers (`system_a.py`, `system_b.py`, `system_c.py`) return raw strings keyed by each system's column names—no value conversion, only CSV shape parsing.\n\n### **The Normalized Record Structure**\n\nEvery record becomes a `Record` with 7 fields: `record_id`, `source_system` (A/B/C), `date` (datetime.date), `account_code`, `account_name`, `description`, `amount` (Decimal dollars).\n\n**Critical conversions happen at read time, not later:**\n- System B: Use `system_b.to_major_units()` to convert integer cents to `Decimal` dollars\n- System C: Parse date as dd/mm/yyyy (reversed from A and B)\n- All codes: uppercase, all amounts: Decimal (never float), account names from `mapping.account_name()` or config's `unknown_account_label`\n\n### **The Five Commands**\n\n1. **`ingest FILE [FILE ...] --out PATH`**: Merge any mix of A/B/C exports into one CSV with header `record_id,source_system,date,account_code,account_name,description,amount`. Rows sorted by date, then system, then record_id. Outputs summary line and exits 0.\n\n2. **`report --by account|month --records PATH --include-refunds`**: Read normalized CSV, print totals per account code (ascending) or per month (ascending). Report decimals per config. Refunds excluded by default (negative amounts).\n\n3. **`reconcile --records PATH --tolerance N`**: Find account/month combos where 2+ systems disagree by more than tolerance. Output `MISMATCH` lines with spread and per-system totals, then count. Tolerance defaults to config value.\n\n4. **`validate FILE [FILE ...]`**: Check exports for: field count mismatch, unparseable dates, unparseable amounts, account codes that don't match `validate.account_code_pattern` (default `^[0-9]{4}$`). Log warnings, output checked/rejected counts, exit 2 if any rejected, else 0.\n\n5. **`--config PATH` (global option)**: Read settings from PATH instead of defaults, falls back to config/settings.toml then built-in defaults. No new files under `config/`.\n\n### **Key Implementation Constraints**\n\n- **Money**: Always `Decimal`, never `float`. Convert to dollars at read time (System B cents → dollars). Round totals half-to-even (Decimal's default).\n- **Output**: Only `cli.emit()` prints; library code returns values. Log warnings through `get_logger(__name__)`.\n- **Annotations**: Every public function must have full type annotations on all parameters and return.\n- **No**: new dependencies, `utils.cache` imports, `legacy_parser` use, `print()` in library code, files under `config/`.\n- **Dates**: All `datetime.date`. Each parser knows its own format; callers handle System C's dd/mm/yyyy.\n- **Flag names are fixed**: `--out`, `--by`, `--records`, `--include-refunds`, `--tolerance`, `--config`.\n\n### **Infrastructure You Already Have**\n\n- `detect_system(path)` → detects which system wrote a file\n- `read_rows(path)` → auto-detects and reads any system's rows as raw strings\n- `normalize(records, keep_refunds=False)` → cleans, filters, sorts records\n- `mapping.account_name(code, unknown_label)` → looks up account name\n- `config.load_settings()` → loads layered settings with no arguments\n- `cli.emit(line)` → the only output function\n- Record.sort_key() → the ordering for all normalized output\n- `fields.split_record()` and `fields.join_record()` → CSV line parsing with quoting", "ttft_ms": 1752, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 58207, "uuid": "3fe1ac17-56c3-4231-9773-d4b5628e0a3e", "ttft_stream_ms": 794, "time_to_request_ms": 142, "first_content_frame_ms": 1013, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-1-task", "_wall_s": 59.6, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
