rns `Decimal` dollars\n  - This is the \"two importers have been caught\" mistake the codebase warns about\n- **System C**: Decimal dollars (386.54, 104.43) ✓ ready to use\n\n### Dates\n\n- **System A**: ISO format YYYY-MM-DD (2026-01-03) ✓ ready to use\n- **System B**: ISO format YYYY-MM-DD (2026-01-07) ✓ ready to use\n- **System C**: **Day-first dd/mm/yyyy** (02/01/2026 = Feb 1, not Jan 2) ✗ **must convert**\n  - The system_c.py code explicitly warns: \"Read month first and the rows past the twelfth of a month blow up, while the rows on or before it quietly land in the wrong month\"\n  - Must parse as `datetime.strptime(raw_string, \"%d/%m/%Y\").date()`\n\n**Summary:** When building a `Record` from raw row data, you need to know which system you're reading and apply the right conversions. System B amounts and System C dates are the gotchas—skip the conversion on either and your normalized records will be silently wrong.", "ttft_ms": 6437, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 10574, "uuid": "ae589c2a-14cb-46d8-80dd-ce0a92497c6d", "ttft_stream_ms": 727, "time_to_request_ms": 132, "first_content_frame_ms": 923, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "p1-3-task", "_wall_s": 14.7, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin", "--resume", "314b7485-8b32-439e-9a37-89d2333d37ce"]}
