 cent-based format)\n- Parses dates correctly for each system (System C uses dd/mm/yyyy)\n- Supports quoted fields in System A exports\n- Outputs to configurable path (default: `out/records.csv`)\n- Creates parent directories as needed\n- Includes all postings (no filtering, no deduplication)\n- Rows sorted by date, then source system, then record_id\n\n### 2. **`report` Command**\n- Generates totals by account code or by month\n- Respects `--include-refunds` flag to control whether negative amounts are included\n- Uses configured decimal places for output formatting\n- Default reads from `out/records.csv`\n- Supports custom records file path via `--records`\n- Applies half-to-even rounding per conventions\n\n### 3. **`reconcile` Command**\n- Finds account/month combinations where systems disagree\n- Compares totals between systems, reports spreads exceeding tolerance\n- Supports `--tolerance` flag to control mismatch threshold\n- Defaults to tolerance from config file (0.05 cents)\n- Includes all postings (refunds included)\n\n### 4. **`validate` Command**\n- Checks export files for malformed rows without writing output\n- Validates:\n  - Correct number of fields\n  - Valid dates in the system's format\n  - Valid numeric amounts\n  - Account codes match pattern\n- Reports warnings for each rejected row\n- Exits with code 2 if rejections found, 0 if clean\n\n### 5. **`--config` Global Option**\n- Placed before the subcommand on the command line\n- Overrides default settings from `config/settings.toml`\n- Applies to all commands (version, inspect, ingest, report, reconcile, validate)\n- Supports only the keys it specifies; others fall back to defaults\n\n### Additional Fixes\n- Fixed System A parser to properly handle quoted fields using `fields.split_record()`\n- Added proper error handling for decimal conversion in all parsers\n- All decimal amounts use `Decimal` type (never float) per conventions\n- Uses `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` rounding mode for report totals\n\nAll existing tests continue to pass, and all five features work correctly with the sample data.", "ttft_ms": 3125, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 340867, "uuid": "fba29c5b-9b4b-4ed6-bf26-f4bc903f7f13", "ttft_stream_ms": 813, "time_to_request_ms": 179, "first_content_frame_ms": 1244, "queued_turn_count": 0, "_label": "phase2", "_wall_s": 342.1, "_argv": ["claude", "-p", "--model", "haiku", "--tools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--allowedTools", "Read,Write,Edit,Bash,Grep,Glob", "--disallowedTools", "Agent", "WebFetch", "WebSearch", "--strict-mcp-config", "--setting-sources", "", "--output-format", "json", "--add-dir", "/home/anatoly/llm-intelligence-test/v3/distractors", "--plugin-dir", "/home/anatoly/context-governance-plugin"]}
